DKEX — Ding Key Exchange (KEX + SIG)
================================================================
An authenticated key-exchange protocol that uses the DKEM KEM for key exchange and
ML-DSA (Dilithium) digital signatures for authentication. Algorithm instances
DKEX-128 / DKEX-256 / DKEX-512 use ML-DSA parameter levels 2 / 5 / 5 respectively.

API_PKC Compliance
----------------------------------------------------------------
drng.c/.h and auxfunc.c/.h are taken VERBATIM from the official API_PKC
template (byte-for-byte unchanged). KAT_KEX.c is based on the official interface and
adapted for the multi-pass handshake as permitted by template Note 6 (which explicitly
allows modifying KAT_KEX.c). Per req 3.4(5), ALL hashing/XOF in the DKE core and the
KEX layer go through the auxiliary functions: the KEX KDF calls sm3hash / pseudoXOF,
and the DKE-core matrix generation / noise sampling call pseudoXOF. The hand-vectorized
parallel-SM3 noise-sampling code (sm3x8 / sm3x4) has been physically removed from the
sources. The algorithm is implemented through the programming interface in
KEX_AlgorithmInstance.h; the build scripts use -fcommon. The ML-DSA component
(dilithium/) is the unmodified NIST reference implementation; its internal SHAKE is
intrinsic to the standardized ML-DSA primitive.

The ML-DSA (Dilithium) signature component — role and IP scope
----------------------------------------------------------------
DKEX is a generic authenticated key-exchange construction: it needs a post-quantum
digital-signature scheme as a pluggable building block, used only through the abstract
signature interface in adkex_sig.h. Any conforming post-quantum signature can be
substituted — nothing in the DKEX construction depends on a specific choice. Here that
interface is instantiated, as a concrete worked EXAMPLE, with ML-DSA (FIPS 204) via
adkex_sig_mldsa.c, and the dilithium/ folder is the UNMODIFIED upstream ML-DSA
(Dilithium) reference. It is bundled only so the implementation is self-contained and its
KAT is reproducible from the submitted sources (req 3.4(2)); per req 3.4(6) it is
therefore listed among the files above.
This dilithium/ code is a standardized THIRD-PARTY component. It is NOT an original
contribution of this submission and is not claimed as such: its upstream authors retain
authorship and it is distributed under its own permissive upstream license. It is
consequently OUTSIDE the scope of this submission's intellectual-property statements,
including the B.3 reference/optimized-implementation ownership statement, which cover
only the DKEX-original sources (the DKE KEM core, the KEX/handshake layer, and the
adkex_sig* glue). Replacing dilithium/ with another conforming PQ signature does not
change DKEX.

Folder Structure
----------------------------------------------------------------
Implementations/{Reference,Optimized}_Implementation/DKEX-{128,256,512}/
Implementations/Additional_Implementation/AArch64_NEON/DKEX-{128,256,512}/  (ARM64; see its README)
Implementations/Additional_Implementation/Cortex-M4/DKEX-{128,256,512}/     (Cortex-M4; see its README)
Implementations/README        (this file; README_CN is the additional Chinese version)
Test_Vectors/KAT_KEX_DKEX-{128,256,512}.txt   (reference and optimized outputs match)

Contents of each instance folder
----------------------------------------------------------------
build.sh                    Build script. the DKE core (flat at the instance root) and dilithium/ have colliding header
                            basenames, so each group is compiled separately (with its
                            own -I) and then linked; the KAT is written to output/.
KEX_AlgorithmInstance.c/.h  API_PKC KEX programming interface (multi-pass handshake +
                            signature authentication).
adkex_derand.c/.h           Derandomized protocol state machine; its KDF calls auxfunc.
adkex_sig_mldsa.c adkex_sig.h   Signature-backend abstraction + ML-DSA binding.
ADKEX_parameters.h          Protocol parameters.
KAT_KEX.c                   KAT vector generator (contains main; adapted for multi-pass
                            per Note 6).
ntt/poly/polyvec/dkecpa/dkecca/...  DKE KEM cryptographic core (IND-CPA part; flat at root; same as DKEM).
drng.* auxfunc.*  [official template files; unmodified].
avx2*/ avx2-dkek/   (optimized only) DKE-core AVX2 NTT kernels.
dilithium/                  ML-DSA (Dilithium) NIST reference implementation, unmodified
                            (sign, poly, ntt, reduce, rounding, packing, fips202,
                            symmetric-shake).

Build: enter an instance folder and run `bash build.sh`. The reference implementation
uses -DDKE_FORCE_SCALAR; the optimized implementation builds the DKE core with
-DDKE_AVX2_NTT256_ASM -DDKE_NTT512_PACKED while ML-DSA stays the reference implementation.
Compile macros: DKE_MODE/ADKEX_MODE=128/256/512, DILITHIUM_MODE=2/5/5, DKE_HASH=0, with
-fcommon. The reference and optimized KATs are byte-identical.


File Manifest — brief description of every file (Submission Requirements 3.4(6))
----------------------------------------------------------------
The three instance folders of each variant (e.g. DKEM-128 / DKEM-256 / DKEM-512)
contain the IDENTICAL set of files, differing only in the DKE_MODE parameter; each
distinct file is therefore described once below.

Per-instance source files — present in each Reference_Implementation/<inst>/, Optimized_Implementation/<inst>/, and the Additional .../<inst>/ root (identical across the -128/-256/-512 instances except the DKE_MODE parameter):
    ADKEX_parameters.h                 Protocol parameter sizes (bits) for the KEX/handshake.
    KAT_KEX.c                          Official API_PKC KAT vector generator for KEX (unmodified).
    KEM_AlgorithmInstance.c / KEM_AlgorithmInstance.h ICCS KEM API instance: kem_keygen/kem_enc/kem_dec entry points.
    KEX_AlgorithmInstance.c / KEX_AlgorithmInstance.h ICCS KEX API instance: initiator/responder entry points.
    adkex_derand.c / adkex_derand.h    Derandomized KEX driver (explicit coins, no live RNG) for deterministic KATs.
    adkex_sig.h                        Pluggable post-quantum signature interface for the DKEX handshake.
    adkex_sig_mldsa.c                  Binds the signature interface to the ML-DSA (dilithium) primitive (DKEX).
    auxfunc.c / auxfunc.h              Official API_PKC auxiliary functions: SM3 / pseudoXOF / pseudohash (unmodified).
    build.sh                           Automated build + KAT-generation script for the instance (Submission Req. 3.4(2)).
    dke_hash.c / dke_hash.h            Hash abstraction; routes all hashing/XOF to the auxfunc SM3 (DKE_HASH=0).
    dke_sm3.c / dke_sm3.h              SM3-based hash/XOF helper wrappers used by the scheme.
    dke_utils.c / dke_utils.h          Miscellaneous byte/bit utility helpers.
    dkecca.c                           IND-CCA KEM via the Fujisaki-Okamoto transform (implicit rejection).
    dkecca.h                           IND-CCA KEM interface header (FO transform).
    dkecpa.c / dkecpa.h                IND-CPA public-key encryption (keygen / encrypt / decrypt).
    drng.c / drng.h                    Official API_PKC deterministic RNG (byte-identical to template; unmodified).
    fips202.h                          SHA-3/SHAKE header; used only by the DKEX ML-DSA path, gated off in the DKE core.
    fips202x4.h                        4-way SHAKE header; used only by the ML-DSA path, gated off in the DKE core.
    ntt.c / ntt.h                      Number-Theoretic Transform: forward/inverse NTT, zeta tables, base multiply.
    packing.c / packing.h              Serialize/deserialize public keys, secret keys and ciphertexts.
    parameters.h                       Unified parameter header; all sizes derived from DKE_MODE (128/256/512).
    poly.c / poly.h                    Single-polynomial arithmetic (add/sub, NTT domain, compress/decompress, CBD).
    polyvec.c / polyvec.h              Vector-of-polynomials arithmetic (basemul-accumulate, compress/decompress).
    random_sampling.c / random_sampling.h Noise / uniform sampling (centered-binomial, rejection).
    randombytes.c / randombytes.h      RNG interface used by the KAT driver (seeded via the API_PKC DRNG).
    reduce.c / reduce.h                Modular reduction (Montgomery / Barrett).
    sm3.c / sm3.h                      SM3 hash core.
    verify.c / verify.h                Constant-time comparison and conditional move (FO transform).

Optimized_Implementation/<inst>/avx2/ — x86-64 AVX2 C kernels & constants:
    consts512_avx2.c                   AVX2 constant tables for the N=512 ring.
    consts_avx2.c                      AVX2 zeta/twiddle constant tables (from pq-crystals/mlkem).
    consts_dkek.h                      Header for the vendored DKEK NTT constants.
    ntt_avx2.c                         AVX2 forward-NTT C glue (vendored ML-KEM).
    poly_avx2.c                        AVX2 polynomial helpers (adapted from pq-crystals/mlkem).
    rejsample_avx2.c                   AVX2 rejection sampling (ported from ML-KEM rejsample.c).
    verify_avx2.c                      AVX2 constant-time verify / conditional move.

Optimized_Implementation/<inst>/{avx2-512, avx2-512p, avx2-dkek}/ — x86-64 AVX2 assembly NTT backends (packed-512 & vendored DKEK):
    align.h                            Memory-alignment macros.
    basemul.S                          AVX2 assembly: pointwise base multiplication.
    consts.c                           AVX2 constant tables (zetas / Montgomery factors) for this NTT backend.
    consts.h                           Header for the AVX2 constant tables.
    fq.S                               AVX2 assembly: Montgomery reduction kernel.
    fq.inc                             AVX2 reduction macro include.
    invntt.S                           AVX2 assembly: inverse NTT kernel.
    ntt.S                              AVX2 assembly: forward NTT kernel.
    ntt512.S                           AVX2 assembly: N=512 forward NTT.
    p512_consts.h                      Packed-512 AVX2 constant declarations.
    p512_fq.inc                        Packed-512 AVX2 reduction macro include.
    p512_params.h                      Packed-512 AVX2 parameters.
    p512_shuffle.inc                   Packed-512 AVX2 shuffle macro include.
    params.h                           Parameters for the vendored AVX2 NTT backend.
    reduce.h                           Packed-domain Montgomery reduction (from pq-crystals/PQClean).
    shuffle.S                          AVX2 assembly: vector lane shuffle helpers.
    shuffle.inc                        AVX2 shuffle macro include.

Optimized_Implementation/<inst>/avx2-linux/ — x86-64 NTT assembly (DKE-original by proposal-team member Liu Rui（刘锐）; the *_dkek_*.S and ntt_tobytes_avx2.S files are pq-crystals ML-KEM ports — third-party, OUTSIDE B.3):
    basemul512_avx2.S                  AVX2 assembly: base multiplication (N=512).
    basemul_avx2.S                     AVX2 assembly: base multiplication (N=256).
    basemul_dkek_avx2.S                AVX2 assembly: base multiplication — PORTED from pq-crystals ML-KEM (third-party, OUTSIDE B.3).
    dke_fq.inc                         AVX2 reduction macro include.
    invntt256_avx2.S                   AVX2 assembly: N=256 inverse NTT.
    invntt512_avx2.S                   AVX2 assembly: N=512 inverse NTT.
    invntt_dkek_avx2.S                 AVX2 assembly: inverse NTT — PORTED from pq-crystals ML-KEM (third-party, OUTSIDE B.3).
    ntt256_avx2.S                      AVX2 assembly: N=256 forward NTT (team-original).
    ntt512_avx2.S                      AVX2 assembly: N=512 forward NTT.
    ntt_avx2_asm.h                     Prototypes for the avx2-linux assembly routines.
    ntt_dkek_avx2.S                    AVX2 assembly: forward NTT — PORTED from pq-crystals ML-KEM (third-party, OUTSIDE B.3).
    ntt_large512_avx2.S                AVX2 assembly: large-coefficient N=512 NTT variant.
    ntt_large_avx2.S                   AVX2 assembly: large-coefficient NTT variant.
    ntt_tobytes_avx2.S                 AVX2 assembly: NTT (de)serialization — PORTED from pq-crystals ML-KEM (third-party, OUTSIDE B.3).
    ntt_unrolled_avx2.S                AVX2 assembly: unrolled NTT variant.
    poly_ops_avx2.S                    AVX2 assembly: polynomial add/sub/reduce helpers.

Additional_Implementation/AArch64_NEON/<inst>/aarch64/ — NEON-intrinsic C kernels:
    fips202x2_neon.h                   2-way SHAKE (NEON) header.
    neon_params.h                      NEON build parameters.
