Third-party code - provenance and IP scope (Optimized AVX2 / Additional NEON & M4)
----------------------------------------------------------------
On the ring shared with the standardized ML-KEM (FIPS 203), the optimized and additional
implementations reuse or adapt several low-level building blocks from public third-party
code. Each is attributed inline at the top of its file:
  Optimized (x86-64 AVX2):
    avx2/consts_avx2.c, avx2/ntt_avx2.c,
    avx2/poly_avx2.c, avx2/rejsample_avx2.c   AVX2 constants / forward NTT / polynomial
                                              helpers / rejection sampling, from
                                              pq-crystals/mlkem.
    avx2-512p/consts.c, p512_consts.h,
    avx2-512p/reduce.h                        packed-domain constants + Montgomery reduce,
                                              from pq-crystals/mlkem and PQClean (mlkem-768).
    random_sampling.c                         AVX2 centered-binomial (CBD) sampling, from
                                              the ML-KEM AVX2 reference.
    avx2-dkek/                                parameters/glue for the vendored ML-KEM /
                                              ntt256 AVX2 NTT asm.
  Additional (arm64 NEON):
    Additional_Implementation/.../aarch64-native/   NTT/inverse-NTT/basemul/reduce assembly
                                              adapted from the mlkem-native project (Arm
                                              Limited / Hanno Becker / Amin Abdulrahman /
                                              Matthias Kannwischer et al.), Apache-2.0 OR
                                              ISC OR MIT.
  Additional (Cortex-M4):
    Additional_Implementation/.../cortex-m4/  Plantard NTT assembly by proposal-team member
                                              Junhao Huang (ePrint 2022/956), Apache-2.0.
License: each component's license identifier is noted inline above and in its source-file
header; full license texts are available from the named upstream projects (and, for the
self-assessment package, the Dependency Statement / 依赖说明).
IP scope - B.3 ownership statement:
  * OUTSIDE B.3 (external third-party, upstream authors retain copyright): the AVX2 blocks
    above from pq-crystals / PQClean, the arm64 NEON assembly from mlkem-native, and the avx2-linux/ *_dkek_*.S + ntt_tobytes_avx2.S ports of pq-crystals ML-KEM. These
    are standardized, openly published components, not an original contribution of this
    submission and not claimed as such.
  * WITHIN B.3 (original to the proposal team): the DKE algorithm design, the portable
    Reference implementation, the hand-written DKE-specific x86-64 NTT assembly under avx2-linux/
    (ntt/invntt/basemul/poly_ops, by proposal-team member Liu Rui（刘锐）; the avx2-linux/
    *_dkek_*.S and ntt_tobytes_avx2.S there are pq-crystals ML-KEM ports — OUTSIDE B.3),
    the Cortex-M4 Plantard NTT assembly (by proposal-team
    member Junhao Huang, ePrint 2022/956), and the protocol / KEX glue.
The portable Reference implementation contains NO external third-party code (plain ISO C99).
Replacing these kernels with another conforming implementation does not change the algorithm.
